# {project} — SDD project

This repository uses **Spec-Driven Development (SDD)**. Before acting, read in order:

1. `sdd/sdd.yaml` — config, profile, runtime facts (if missing, run `SDD: init` first)
2. `sdd/agents/README.md` — agent roster: roles, mandatory reading, allowed writes
3. `sdd/constitution.md` — principles · `sdd/guardrails.md` — architecture invariants
4. `sdd/specs/` — active work. **Never code without an explicitly authorized task.**

## Locks
{locks}

## Working
Assume the agent role the task names (file in `sdd/agents/`); its Mandatory Reading and
Forbidden sections and `sdd/agents/capability-matrix.yaml` are binding.

## Commands
`SDD: init` · `SDD: spec <id>` · `SDD: implement <id> TASK-<n>[, ...]` · `SDD: review <id>` · `SDD: finish <id>`
(VS Code: `/sdd-*` prompt files · Claude Code: `/sdd-*` commands · Codex: `sdd-*` skills)

## Git & commits
Follow `sdd/gitflow.md` (project-owned — the team may customize it). Detect which agentic
runtime you are (Claude Code, Copilot, Codex, Devin) and sign commits with the trailer that
file defines for your runtime. Never commit without an authorized task; never force-push.
